# fast08.env -- the ISPD 2024 runtime mechanisms (Parts 116-120) applied to
# the ISPD 2008 standard, layered on @standard.env (HISTORY_COST_SWEEP.md
# Part 124). Part of the 2008 standard since 2026-10-14 (Part 124's
# sixteen runs: zero-overflow designs 31-70% faster, residues +4 to +10).
# The 2008 standard: <name> bench/<design>.gr ./pd39route @standard.env @fast08.env
#
# Exact (the same routes at any thread count, Parts 116 and 120): worker
# threads, and the pattern stage's batches on the dependency graph. On the
# 2008 designs the pattern stage is ~0.2% of the run, so these buy little.
PD37ROUTE_THREADS=8
PD38ROUTE_PATTERN_DAG=1
# Not exact (Parts 118-119; judged on overflow and wirelength here): the
# slow tier in batches of 256 drawn round-robin from 64 x 64-tile areas,
# searched in parallel against snapshots and committed in net order. The
# slow tier is ~28% of a 2008 run (newblue4: 2691 of 9504 s).
PD38ROUTE_SLOW_BATCH=256
PD38ROUTE_SLOW_SPREAD=64
# Not applied: the region stage, refinement and the reclaim fallback stay
# on (2008 needs them to reach zero overflow; the 2024 pipeline dropped
# them, so nothing threads them yet -- ~70% of a 2008 run). The 3D pattern
# passes (PD38ROUTE_P3D_REUSE) are a 2024-only stage.
#
# The late-stage portfolio (Part 135, adopted 2026-10-19): when path A (region
# stage + refinement, the run's own settings) ends above the fallback
# threshold (10) -- the residue designs, where the reclaim path is skipped --
# path A is rerun from its start state with Lagrangian multipliers at steps
# 0.05 / 0.2 / 1, each on its own thread, and the best by (overflow, 2D wire)
# is kept. Designs ending at or below 10 run no variants (the same routes, no
# extra cost). Residues: newblue1 30 -> 24, newblue4 154 -> 140, bigblue4
# 366 -> 360, newblue3 38948 -> 38898, newblue7 104 -> 104.
PD39ROUTE_PORTFOLIO=lagr=0.05;lagr=0.2;lagr=1
PD39ROUTE_PORTFOLIO_WHEN=after
#
# The region stage's early stop (Part 146, adopted 2026-10-22): when more than 1000 units of 2D overflow
# enter the region stage and its best is still not below its start after 20 rounds, it stops there (and the
# portfolio's variants are skipped). Every stage it stopped would have returned its start anyway: on the
# four tightened variants tested the routes were byte-identical and the runs 31-48% faster. On the sixteen
# benchmarks only newblue3 enters above 1000, and its region stage is below its start by round 20, so the
# 2008 standard's routes are unchanged.
PD39ROUTE_REGION_ABORT=1000,20
